---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../content/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy — ${site.name}`}
  description={`Privacy policy for ${site.name}, a live sports audio control app for iOS.`}
>
  <article class="section container prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Last updated: June 9, 2026</p>

    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is a live sports audio control app for iPhone and iPad. It is built to be
      private by design: {site.name} does not require an account and collects no personal
      data. This policy explains what stays on your device, how the optional features work,
      and the choices you have.
    </p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} collects no personal information and transmits none to any server. Everything
      you create in the app — team rosters, player names and jersey numbers, sound cues, boards,
      scripts, setlists, and app settings — is stored only on your device. {site.name} has no
      accounts, no sign-in, and no backend.
    </p>

    <h2>Local Audio Files and Imported Content</h2>
    <p>
      Audio files you import and clips you record remain in {site.name}'s on-device storage.
      {site.name} does not upload, transmit, or share your audio with any server or third party.
    </p>

    <h2>Microphone</h2>
    <p>
      If you choose to record audio clips, {site.name} uses the microphone solely to create
      those recordings. Recordings are saved locally on your device and are never transmitted.
      You can grant or revoke microphone access at any time in iOS Settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Apple Music Integration</h2>
    <p>
      Apple Music is optional. If you authorize it, {site.name} uses Apple's MusicKit framework
      to let you search the catalog and your library and assign tracks to sound cues. This is
      read-only access provided through Apple; {site.name} does not collect, store, or transmit
      your Apple Music credentials, listening history, or playback activity. Your Apple Music
      account is managed by iOS and is subject to
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/data/en/apple-music/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Backup and Export</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} can save your setup to a backup file stored on your device. You may then export
      that file to a location you choose — for example, the Files app or iCloud Drive. {site.name}
      does not automatically upload or sync your data to any cloud service or server; exporting and
      where the file goes are entirely under your control.
    </p>

    <h2>In-App Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} Pro is purchased through the Apple App Store using StoreKit. Apple processes the
      transaction; {site.name} never receives or stores your payment information. Purchases are
      governed by
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/en-ww/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics, Diagnostics, and Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} contains no third-party analytics, crash reporting, advertising, or tracking
      software. It does not collect usage data and does not track you across other apps or
      websites.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} relies on only the following Apple services, each governed by its own privacy
      policy:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Apple Music — optional, for assigning and playing catalog tracks as cues</li>
      <li>Apple App Store / StoreKit — for the optional Pro purchase</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data Retention and Your Choices</h2>
    <p>
      Because all data is stored locally, retention is under your control. You can:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use {site.name} fully without connecting Apple Music or any external service.</li>
      <li>Delete all data by removing the app from your device.</li>
      <li>Grant or revoke Apple Music and microphone permissions in iOS Settings.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is intended for game-day operators and is not directed to children under 13.
      Because {site.name} collects no personal information from anyone, it knowingly collects no
      personal information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this privacy policy, contact us at
      <a href={`mailto:${site.privacyEmail}`}>{site.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with
      an updated revision date.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .last-updated {
    font-size: var(--small);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
</style>
